Let $\rho$ be the diagonal embedding of $\tilde{W}_\#$ into $\mathbb{H}_\#\otimes C(V)$;
$$\rho (w) = p(w) \otimes w, \text{ for all } w \in \tilde{W}_\#.$$
Hence, for an $\mathbb{H}_\#$-module $X$ and a spinor module $\mathcal{S}$, we can consider $X\otimes \mathcal{S}$ as a $\tilde{W}_\#$-module via the map $\rho$.

